SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Summary: Skip the int 68h/41h SoftICE probes that Wine's macOS code segment provokes (Armadillo DRM)
Category: cpu
Kind: workaround
Origin: wine-mac-builds
From: written for wine-mac-builds. Behaviour of Second Chance's binary patch
 of 32-bit ntdll (RosettaFaultFix, part 2), done in the Unix-side fault
 handler beside 0040 (which is part 1).
Source: none published
Upstream: no
Why: On macOS Wine runs 32-bit code in an LDT code segment (cs 0x107), not
 NT's 0x23. Armadillo, the DRM in Big Fish games, tells Windows 9x from NT
 by the high byte of %cs, so under Wine it takes the 9x path and probes for
 the SoftICE debugger with "int 68h" (and "int 41h"). On a real 9x without
 SoftICE those do nothing; here they fault. In Armadillo's child process
 the fault goes to its debugger (the parent), whose debugger thread is
 meanwhile in WaitForInputIdle on the child, so the launcher stalls and the
 game never starts. Only in that LDT code segment, step over int 68h/41h
 as 9x would. On NT they'd fault, but no NT program runs in that segment
 expecting that: the segment is what makes these checks misfire.
Applies to: wine 11.21 (macfixes, after 0052)
Status: not yet built. Second Chance's binary patch, which does the same,
 makes White Wolf's launcher (wqxgxgg.exe) start the game on
 macfixes-10.0-build3; without it the launcher stalls.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
index 9553ebf..264e98c 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -2041,6 +2041,29 @@ static BOOL emulate_fs_addr32( struct thread_data *data, ucontext_t *sigcontext
     TRACE_(seh)( "emulated an fs: addr32 instruction (%02x) at %#x\n", instr[2], (DWORD)(RIP_sig(sigcontext) - len) );
     return TRUE;
 }
+
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           skip_9x_debugger_probe
+ *
+ * On macOS, 32-bit code runs in an LDT code segment (cs32_sel, e.g. 0x107)
+ * instead of NT's 0x23. Programs that tell Windows 9x from NT by the high
+ * byte of %cs (Armadillo, the DRM in Big Fish games, does) decide they're
+ * on 9x and probe for the SoftICE debugger with "int 68h" or "int 41h".
+ * On a real 9x without SoftICE those do nothing; here they fault, and
+ * Armadillo's debugger-protected child stalls on the exception. Only in
+ * that LDT segment, step over them as 9x would.
+ */
+static BOOL skip_9x_debugger_probe( ucontext_t *sigcontext )
+{
+    BYTE instr[2];
+
+    if (!cs32_sel || CS_sig(sigcontext) != cs32_sel) return FALSE;
+    if (virtual_uninterrupted_read_memory( (BYTE *)(ULONG_PTR)(DWORD)RIP_sig(sigcontext), instr, 2 ) != 2) return FALSE;
+    if (instr[0] != 0xcd || (instr[1] != 0x68 && instr[1] != 0x41)) return FALSE;
+    TRACE_(seh)( "skipped int %02xh (9x debugger probe) at %#x\n", instr[1], (DWORD)RIP_sig(sigcontext) );
+    RIP_sig(sigcontext) += 2;
+    return TRUE;
+}
 #endif
 
 /***********************************************************************
@@ -2562,6 +2585,11 @@ static void segv_handler( int signal, siginfo_t *siginfo, void *_sigcontext )
                 leave_handler( data, sigcontext );
                 return;
             }
+            if (skip_9x_debugger_probe( sigcontext ))
+            {
+                leave_handler( data, sigcontext );
+                return;
+            }
 #endif
             if (!err && (rec.ExceptionCode = is_privileged_instr( &context.c ))) break;
             if ((err & 7) == 2 && handle_interrupt( data, sigcontext, &rec, &context )) return;
